<article class="env-lemma" id="06DN">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06DN">Lemma <span data-tag="06DN">67.6.6</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $p : X \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k)$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$ where $k$ is a field. Then $p : X \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k)$ is universally open. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose a scheme $U$ and a surjective étale morphism $U \to X$. The composition $U \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k)$ is universally open (as a morphism of schemes) by Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/0383" data-tag="0383">29.24.4</a>. Let $Z \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k)$ be a morphism of schemes. Then $U \times _{\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k)} Z \to X \times _{\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k)} Z$ is surjective, see Lemma <a href="/tag/03MH" data-tag="03MH">67.5.5</a>. Hence the first of the maps 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  |U \times _{\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k)} Z| \to |X \times _{\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k)} Z| \to |Z|  \]
</div>
    <p>
       is surjective. Since the composition is open by the above we conclude that the second map is open as well. Whence $p$ is universally open by Lemma <a href="/tag/03Z5" data-tag="03Z5">67.6.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>